Bar Manager FAQ: Setting up Square POS API with the Platform
============================================================

Q: What is the Square POS API?
------------------------------

A: The Square POS API is an interface provided by Square that allows third-party applications to integrate with Square Point of Sale (POS) software. By integrating the Platform with Square POS, you can synchronize sales data, manage inventory, and process payments from within the Platform.

Q: How do I set up my Square POS API with the Platform?
-------------------------------------------------------

A: To set up your Square POS API with the Platform, follow these steps:

1. Log in to your Square Developer Dashboard and create a new application.
2. Obtain your application ID and personal access token from the Square Developer Dashboard.
3. Log in to the Platform and navigate to the Manage API Access page.
4. Enter your application ID and personal access token in the form on the Manage API Access page and click "Create Integration".
5. If you already have a Square POS integration set up, you can edit your application ID and access token on the Manage API Access page.

Q: How do I obtain my Square application ID and personal access token?
----------------------------------------------------------------------

A: To obtain your Square application ID and personal access token, follow these steps:

1. Log in to your Square Developer Dashboard.
2. Select the application that you want to integrate with the Platform.
3. Click on the "Credentials" tab.
4. Copy your application ID and personal access token from the "Sandbox Access Token" section.

Q: What if I don't have a Square Developer account?
---------------------------------------------------

A: You can sign up for a Square Developer account for free on the Square Developer website. Once you have signed up, you can create a new application and obtain your application ID and personal access token.
