In a linked list set, the time complexity of removal is `O(n)`, because the set is implemented as a linked list and removal requires searching for the element in the list and then updating the pointers to remove it.

Overall, the time complexity of removal in a set data structure depends on the specific implementation of the set and can vary from `O(1)` to `O(n)`.
