why is the type:"post" when im only getting the search results?
The type "POST" is used in the AJAX call because it is more secure than "GET" and it is considered best practice to use it when sending sensitive information such as user input to the server.
Even though you are only retrieving the search results, the user input (dvdTitle, maxPrice and category) is still being sent to the server and it is considered as sensitive data.
Using "POST" ensures that this data is not exposed in the URL and it's not cached by the browser. This can prevent attackers from intercepting the data and it also keeps the user input private.

Also, by using "POST" you can tell the server that you want to create or update something and the server can manage that accordingly.

You can use GET if the data that you are sending to the server is not sensitive and you don't mind the data being exposed in the URL.

In short, "POST" is preferred when sending sensitive data, such as user input, to the server while "GET" is preferred when retrieving non-sensitive data from the server.
