how would I create a isValidToken() function?
A function called `isValidToken()` can be created to check if a JSON web token is valid. It can be implemented as follows:
```
function isValidToken() {
    // Get the token from storage
    var token = localStorage.getItem("token");

    // If the token does not exist, return false
    if (!token) {
        return false;
    }

    // Split the token by '.' to get the header, payload and signature
    var parts = token.split('.');

    // If the token is not composed of 3 parts, return false
    if (parts.length !== 3) {
        return false;
    }

    // Decode the token and parse it as JSON
    var decoded = JSON.parse(atob(parts[1]));

    // Check if the token has expired
    var expiry = decoded.exp;
    if (expiry < Date.now() / 1000) {
        return false;
    }

    // If the token is valid and has not expired, return true
    return true;
}
```
This function will check for the existence of a token in the local storage, check if the token is composed of 3 parts, decode the token and parse it as JSON and check if the token has expired.

You can then call this function to check the token and show or hide elements based on the result.
