how do I remove the history of previous pages?
There are a few ways to remove the history of previous pages depending on the context of your application.

1. You can use the `window.history.replaceState()` method to replace the current page with a new page, effectively removing the previous page from the browser's history.
2. You can also use the `window.history.pushState()` method to add new pages to the browser's history, while removing the previous pages.
3. You can disable the back button of the browser using javascript, this way the user will not be able to go back to previous pages.
4. Another option is to use the `sessionStorage` or `localStorage` API to store the current page's state, and then clear it when the user navigates to a new page.
5. You can also use the `window.location.replace()` method instead of `window.location.href`, this will replace the current page on the history stack and the user will not be able to go back.
6. Use `window.location.href = "about:blank"` . This will load an empty page and the user will not be able to go back to the previous page.

It is important to note that some of these methods may not work as intended if the user has certain browser extensions or settings enabled, such as "Privacy Badger" which blocks some javascripts.
